The Texecom Connect protocol support in this folder was written for this
project. The framing, CRC parameters, command numbers and message layouts
follow the publicly released Python implementation:

  texecom-connect - Copyright (C) 2018 Joseph Heenan
  https://github.com/davidMbrooke/texecom-connect
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

That implementation was written using information Texecom provided under
NDA; Texecom confirmed (8 June 2018) that the program could be released.
No Texecom documentation is reproduced here.

Arming, disarming, resetting and the zone-state / area-flag reads (command
numbers, arm types, area bitmap and flag layouts, and the "reset before
disarm when in alarm" behaviour) are adapted from texecom2mqtt 1.3.1:

  texecom2mqtt - Copyright (c) 2020 Daniel Chesterton
  https://github.com/dchesterton/texecom2mqtt-hassio
  MIT License - see LICENSE-texecom2mqtt in this folder

The arm/disarm/reset and zone-state / area-flag command layouts were also
cross-checked against an independently maintained, Apache-2.0 licensed
fork of texecom-connect (https://github.com/Sjoerdfc/texecom-connect), whose
idle-time state re-read is the model for the keep-alive here. Area flag
numbers beyond texecom2mqtt's (17/18 Entry, 19 Exit, 24 Part Arming) and the
behaviour of firmware that refuses bulk area-flag reads come from a further
Apache-2.0 fork: https://github.com/southseaboy/texecom-connect

Handling of NAK replies to reads (the panel refuses commands right after a
burst of events; taken as data a 0x15 reads as "zone active" or "area in
alarm") follows real-panel observations published by michaelmarconi/
texecom_alarm (MIT): https://github.com/michaelmarconi/texecom_alarm

Other behaviour (timings, session drops during alarm reporting, unknown
area state 6, event type 137) was observed on a real Premier Elite panel
during testing for this project.
